// document_generation_live.jsonl — issue #413: office-document generation across every format
// Chad claims to support (docx/xlsx/pptx via the code_execution skills in src/skills/{docx,
// xlsx,pptx}, pdf via typst). Companion to visual_artifacts_live.jsonl (which already covers
// compile_typst/render_diagram/render_marp/render_animation/generate_presentation) — this fills
// the docx/xlsx/manual-pptx gap specifically. All three run through sandboxed code execution
// (delegate_to_code_agent / run_sandboxed_python / run_sandboxed_bash), NOT a dedicated native
// tool, so assertions are looser (judge-led) than a single fixed tool name. LIVE lane only.
{"id": "docx_report_live", "prompt": "write a 1-page Word document (.docx) summarizing the key differences between REST and GraphQL APIs, with a heading and a short bulleted list", "category": "agent", "expect": {"tools_any": ["delegate_to_code_agent", "run_sandboxed_python", "run_sandboxed_bash", "write_file", "load_skill"], "response_excludes": ["i cannot", "i don't have access"], "max_duration_s": 180}, "judge": ["tool_appropriateness", "response_grounded"], "note": "docx skill has never been exercised by any live dataset; confirms load_skill('docx') -> docx-js -> a real downloadable .docx artifact"}
{"id": "xlsx_budget_template_live", "prompt": "create an Excel spreadsheet (.xlsx) with a simple monthly budget template: columns for Category, Budgeted, Actual, and a Difference column that's a formula (Budgeted minus Actual), with 5 example category rows", "category": "agent", "expect": {"tools_any": ["delegate_to_code_agent", "run_sandboxed_python", "run_sandboxed_bash", "write_file", "load_skill"], "max_duration_s": 180}, "judge": ["tool_appropriateness", "response_grounded"], "note": "xlsx skill untested end-to-end; formula requirement checks the deliverable is a real spreadsheet with working formulas, not just a table pasted as text"}
{"id": "xlsx_messy_data_cleanup_live", "prompt": "I have a messy list of expenses with inconsistent formatting: 'Coffee - $4.50', '12.00 (lunch)', 'Gas: 35', 'movie tix $22.5'. Turn this into a clean Excel spreadsheet with Item, Amount, and a total row.", "category": "agent", "expect": {"tools_any": ["delegate_to_code_agent", "run_sandboxed_python", "run_sandboxed_bash", "write_file", "load_skill"], "max_duration_s": 180}, "judge": ["tool_appropriateness", "response_grounded"], "note": "messy-data-restructuring path called out explicitly in the xlsx skill description; checks numeric extraction/normalization, not just literal copy"}
{"id": "pptx_manual_skill_live", "prompt": "using python-pptx directly (not any AI slide generator), create a simple 5-slide pptx presentation about the history of pizza: title, origins, spread to America, modern variations, closing", "category": "agent", "expect": {"tools_any": ["delegate_to_code_agent", "run_sandboxed_python", "run_sandboxed_bash", "write_file", "load_skill"], "max_duration_s": 180}, "judge": ["tool_appropriateness", "response_grounded"], "note": "the pptx SKILL.md's manual code-execution path (pptxgenjs/python-pptx) is distinct from generate_presentation/Presenton (covered in mcp_untested_live.jsonl) -- both routes need independent coverage since they hit completely different code"}
{"id": "pdf_multi_section_report_live", "prompt": "create a 2-page PDF report with a title page and a section comparing 3 project management tools (Trello, Asana, Linear) in a table", "category": "agent", "expect": {"tools_any": ["compile_typst"], "tools_exclude": ["createTextFile", "uploadFile"], "max_duration_s": 180}, "judge": ["tool_appropriateness", "response_grounded"], "note": "heavier PDF case than visual_artifacts_live.jsonl's 1-page spikeball case -- multi-section + a real table, closer to what users actually ask for"}
{"id": "docx_to_pdf_export_request_live", "prompt": "write a short one-page cover letter as a Word document, then also give me a PDF version of it", "category": "agent", "expect": {"max_duration_s": 200}, "judge": ["tool_appropriateness", "response_grounded"], "note": "cross-format chain (docx skill then either a docx->pdf conversion step or a second typst pass) -- checks the agent actually produces BOTH artifacts rather than only the first one mentioned"}
